No Collada module on iOS, for now.

The Collada module is a shared library that DllLoader opens with dlopen at
runtime to convert raw .dae art into the engine's own formats. It is not linked
into pyrogenesis - but the main project carries `dependson { "Collada" }`, so
`make pyrogenesis` builds it anyway, and it needs FCollada, which wants Carbon's
MPCriticalRegionID. That does not exist on iOS.

Leaving it out costs nothing for playing: the shipped game data is already
converted, and the engine only complains about a missing module when a mod
ships .dae files. Getting it back means patching FCollada's critical section to
use pthreads and putting the .dylib where dlopen finds it - inside the bundle in
the simulator, and under Frameworks/ on a device. Worth doing later, not needed
to find out whether the game runs.

